  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734232",
      "title": "Updating the UI Based on Auth Status",
      "sourceHash": "74ca8cbeb72e1df987f14b05634abf0870796a5828eb34a744015b351fe3b15a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "So now to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "based on the existence of the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "I wanna make the token easily available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 11.73,
          "en": "in my entire application on all my routes basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.73,
          "end": 15.54,
          "en": "and I also wanna make sure that the information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.54,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "whether the token exists or not, is automatically updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "so that if the token would be removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "because we log out, the UI automatically updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 28.901,
          "en": "Therefore, for that reason, I don't just wanna call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.901,
          "end": 31.77,
          "en": "getAuthToken, my helper function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.77,
          "end": 33.57,
          "en": "in main navigation, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "to get the token because that function is only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "called when this component is reevaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "but it will not lead to the component being reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "if the token is deleted in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "So I want a more reactive solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 50.61,
          "en": "And we could use React context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.61,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "for managing that token across the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "That would be a perfectly fine way of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 59.4,
          "en": "But since we're using React-router, we can also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.4,
          "end": 64.02,
          "en": "again leverage that tool, that package for doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.02,
          "end": 66.81,
          "en": "And we could, for example, go to our root route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.81,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "which in the end wraps all other routes as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "And there we could add a loader, which simply takes a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 78.81,
          "en": "at local storage and extracts the token from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 81.2,
          "en": "And that token would then be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.2,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "through the loader data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "of that root route in all other routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 88.11,
          "en": "The best thing about that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.11,
          "end": 92.64,
          "en": "that React router will automatically reevaluate that if we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.64,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "for example, log out, if we submit that logout form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 99.42,
          "en": "So it will then re fetch that token and for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.42,
          "end": 101.61,
          "en": "determine that the token doesn't exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.61,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "and then update all the pages that use that loader data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "from that root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 108.99000000000001,
          "en": "So that is a very reactive solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.99000000000001,
          "end": 111.513,
          "en": "and that's therefore why I will use that approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 116.25,
          "en": "So here we can add our loader function and I will put that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.25,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "in a separate file in my off utility file, actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "Here I'll add my tokenLoader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 127.09,
          "en": "And in that function here, I will simply call getAuthToken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "and return the result of calling that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 133.5,
          "en": "So that is quite straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.5,
          "end": 135.603,
          "en": "I will just use that helper function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.5,
          "end": 141.39,
          "en": "But now back in App.js, I will import this loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 146.39,
          "en": "as the tokenLoader from /util/auth and use that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 149.523,
          "en": "on that root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 154.02,
          "en": "So now this will be called whenever a new navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.02,
          "end": 156.933,
          "en": "action occurs, for example, because we triggered a logout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.933,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "and therefore we will check the current status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.23,
          "en": "of the token whenever the user does anything on the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.23,
          "end": 166.29,
          "en": "whenever the user submits a form or navigates around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.29,
          "end": 168.51,
          "en": "And that therefore ensures that we always have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 171.153,
          "en": "the latest information about that token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 175.71,
          "en": "Now, here I have an error because I named this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.71,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "tokenLoader already, so I should import it as tokenLoader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 182.52,
          "en": "And now with that, that should be working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.52,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "So now we can use that loader data from that root route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "in all our other routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 190.44,
          "en": "In order to use data from that loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.44,
          "end": 191.97,
          "en": "and easily get access to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "I'll assign an ID to that route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 196.263,
          "en": "Root sounds like a fitting id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 199.86,
          "en": "And now in MainNavigation.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.86,
          "end": 202.8,
          "en": "we can use this useRouteLoaderData hook about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "which we learned in the routing section already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 210.513,
          "en": "to get our token here by targeting the root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 213.96,
          "en": "And we know that what will get here is the token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.96,
          "end": 215.043,
          "en": "because that is what the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.043,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "that root routes loader does return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 220.863,
          "en": "The tokenLoader here does return the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.18,
          "end": 225.45,
          "en": "So therefore, in MainNavigation, we now get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.45,
          "end": 229.02,
          "en": "of that token and we now know that if that token exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.02,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "we're logged in, and if it does not exist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 233.733,
          "en": "if this is undefined, we're not logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.6,
          "end": 236.67000000000002,
          "en": "Therefore we can conditionally show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.67000000000002,
          "end": 240.51,
          "en": "that authentication link here by checking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.51,
          "end": 244.35,
          "en": "if token exists and only rendering this list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.35,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "if it does exist. Though that would show it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 250.38,
          "en": "if we are locked in and we want the opposite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.38,
          "end": 252.453,
          "en": "hence I'll add an exclamation mark here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 253.41,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "Now that authentication link is only shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 259.08,
          "en": "if we're not logged in, if we don't have a token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.08,
          "end": 259.913,
          "en": "On the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.913,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "that logout button should only be shown if we are logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 264.87,
          "en": "So here I'll have the opposite logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.87,
          "end": 266.58,
          "en": "I'll check if we have a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.58,
          "end": 268.593,
          "en": "and then I'll render this list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.88,
          "end": 273.09000000000003,
          "en": "With that, if I save this uc, I see authentication here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.09000000000003,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "because at the moment I have no token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 277.77,
          "en": "But if I do log in again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.77,
          "end": 282.27,
          "en": "if I do submit that form with valid credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.27,
          "end": 285.293,
          "en": "that changes, and I now see logout instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.26,
          "end": 288.36,
          "en": "And we can use the same approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 288.36,
          "end": 290.85,
          "en": "for conditionally showing these edit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 290.85,
          "end": 293.703,
          "en": "and delete buttons or this new event button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.72,
          "end": 297.93,
          "en": "For that, we can, for example, go to events navigation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.93,
          "end": 301.05,
          "en": "which is where I have this new event button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "and use the exact same approach as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "Use the RouteLoaderData hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 311.1,
          "en": "which is imported from react-router-dom, to get our token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 311.1,
          "end": 313.83,
          "en": "by getting the loader data from the root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.83,
          "end": 318.45,
          "en": "And then we only show this new event link here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 318.45,
          "end": 322.08,
          "en": "if we have a token and not otherwise, because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.08,
          "end": 325.47,
          "en": "if we're not logged in, it makes no sense to show this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.47,
          "end": 327.69,
          "en": "And the same is true for the event item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 327.69,
          "end": 332.46,
          "en": "There, I also will use the useRouteLoaderData hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.46,
          "end": 334.53,
          "en": "to get data from my root route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334.53,
          "end": 336.303,
          "en": "and that data is the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.32,
          "end": 339.54,
          "en": "And that information can now be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.54,
          "end": 341.73,
          "en": "to conditionally show that menu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.73,
          "end": 344.19,
          "en": "Here I only wanna show it if we have a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 344.19,
          "end": 347.733,
          "en": "because otherwise we can't edit or delete this anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 348.75,
          "end": 350.52,
          "en": "So with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 350.52,
          "end": 353.46,
          "en": "I see all these items because I am logged in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 353.46,
          "end": 356.43,
          "en": "but if I log out and I then go back to events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 356.43,
          "end": 358.53,
          "en": "you see the new event button is gone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 358.53,
          "end": 361.77,
          "en": "and also edit and delete are gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 361.77,
          "end": 363.453,
          "en": "So that works as it should.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}